          "source_text_sha256": "7902a521953ef4a4f5bb78c6ba0e6eb2f0b5bdb22958a6d6e14a25ef10a36b95",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: After his work day on August 23, 2023, which ends around 23:00/23:30, the witness decides to go to a gym in Batz-sur-Mer (44) for a nighttime fitness session between 00:30 and 01:30. On his way back to the campsite where he was staying for his vacation, he decided to walk along the coast. Around 1:30/1:40 a.m., while in the vicinity of coordinates 47.27411, -2.482339, he spots a fixed, very bright white light, slightly smaller in size than the Moon. At first intrigued, he thinks for a moment that it could be the Moon, but he is categorical: it was not. Surprised, he calls his cousin who remained at the campsite to tell him what he is observing. His cousin, not impressed, goes back to bed, but he stays at the site for another 20 to 30 minutes, fascinated by this unusual phenomenon. Below, on Saint-Michel beach, he notices a group of 13 to 15-year-old teenagers taking a midnight swim. Around 2 AM, when they leave, he takes the opportunity to go talk to them. They, too, noticed the strange light in the sky and, though they are not particularly interested, they confirm that it is not the Moon. Around 2:30 AM, aware that he needs to work the next morning, the witness leaves the location to go to bed. The bright point was still present, fixed in the sky, when it departed. The consistency* of the case is not optimal, but it remains sufficient to provide a relevant conclusion. The transmitted video could be analyzed, reinforcing the consistency of the case by scripting the observation. According to the criteria of GEIPAN, consistency is the amount of reliable and objective information gathered for a testimony. The case study (see the investigation report) and inquiries with our maritime expert allow us to formally identify the PAN as the powerful lighthouse of the TRITON ship in the area at the time of the observation. The GEIPAN is classified as A: observation of the lighthouse of the ship TRITON.",
